        "    + theme_minimal()\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "aea8546b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Overall, the sample remains large after cleaning and is suitable for machine learning. The missing-value treatment balances data retention with robustness, while the industry recoding keeps the dimensionality of the feature matrix manageable.\n",
        "\n",
        "### 1c: Feature matrix construction\n",
        "The assignment asks for a feature matrix consisting of stock characteristics and all interactions between stock characteristics and macroeconomic variables. With 10 stock characteristics and 4 macro predictors, this yields 10+10×4=50 continuous predictors. We then add industry dummies based on the recoded SIC divisions."
      ],
      "id": "ef00474f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Create stock characteristic × macro interactions\n",
        "interaction_cols = []\n",
        "for s in stock_chars:\n",
        "    for m in macro_vars:\n",
        "        name = f\"{s}_x_{m}\"\n",
        "        df[name] = df[s] * df[m]\n",
        "        interaction_cols.append(name)\n",
        "\n",
        "# One-hot encode broad industry groups\n",
        "sic_dummies = pd.get_dummies(df[\"sic_division\"], prefix=\"sic\", drop_first=True, dtype=int)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Final feature sets\n",
        "continuous_features = stock_chars + interaction_cols\n",
        "dummy_features = list(sic_dummies.columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Build X, y, and metadata objects for later exercises\n",
        "X = pd.concat(\n",
        "    [df[continuous_features].reset_index(drop=True),\n",
        "     sic_dummies.reset_index(drop=True)],\n",
        "    axis=1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "y = df[\"ret_excess\"].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "meta = df[[\"permno\", \"date\", \"mktcap_lag\", \"ret_excess\"]].reset_index(drop=True)"
      ],
      "id": "661b2d56",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "feature_overview = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"object\": [\"X\", \"y\", \"meta\"],\n",
        "    \"shape\": [X.shape, y.shape, meta.shape]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_overview"
      ],
      "id": "c75628f1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"feature_group\": [\"stock characteristics\", \"interaction terms\", \"industry dummies\", \"total features\"],\n",
        "    \"count\": [len(stock_chars), len(interaction_cols), len(dummy_features), X.shape[1]]\n",
        "})"
      ],
      "id": "cbf1e680",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The final feature matrix contains the 10 selected stock characteristics, 40 interaction terms between stock characteristics and macroeconomic variables, and industry dummies for the broad SIC divisions. \n",
        "\n",
        "## Exercise 2\n",
        "### Exercise 2a: Model descriptions\n",
        "\n",
        "**Elastic Net** is a penalized linear regression model that combines the $L_1$ penalty from the Lasso and the $L_2$ penalty from Ridge regression. It minimizes\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\min_{\\beta} \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^N (y_i - x_i'\\beta)^2 + \\alpha \\left( \\lambda \\|\\beta\\|_1 + (1-\\lambda)\\|\\beta\\|_2^2 \\right)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "where the first term is the mean squared prediction error and the second penalizes coefficient size, helping to control overfitting in high-dimensional settings with correlated predictors, as in our feature matrix.\n",
        "\n",
        "The key hyperparameters are the overall penalty strength (`alpha`) and the mixing parameter (`l1_ratio`), where `l1_ratio = 1` corresponds to the Lasso and `l1_ratio = 0` to Ridge.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Neural Network (MLP)** approximates $g(z_{i,t})$ as a composition of linear transformations and nonlinear activation functions across multiple hidden layers. The model is trained by minimizing the mean squared prediction error. Each neuron computes $x_k^l = f\\left(\\theta_0^k + \\sum_j z_j \\theta_j^k\\right)$, where $f$ is the ReLU activation function, and the network is trained via backpropagation.\n",
        "\n",
        "The key hyperparameters are the number and size of hidden layers (`hidden_layer_sizes`), the $L_2$ regularization strength (`alpha`), and the maximum number of iterations (`max_iter`).\n",
        "\n",
        "The two models provide a comparison between a structured, regularized linear benchmark and a more flexible nonlinear model.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise 2b: Time-respecting data split"
      ],
      "id": "29bfe26e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "# Split by unique dates rather than raw rows\n",
        "unique_dates = sorted(meta[\"date\"].unique())\n",
        "\n",
        "n_dates = len(unique_dates)\n",
        "test_start = int(n_dates * 0.80)\n",
        "val_start = int(test_start * 0.75)\n",
        "\n",
        "train_dates = unique_dates[:val_start]\n",
        "val_dates   = unique_dates[val_start:test_start]\n",
        "test_dates  = unique_dates[test_start:]\n",
        "\n",
        "train_mask = meta[\"date\"].isin(train_dates)\n",
        "val_mask   = meta[\"date\"].isin(val_dates)\n",
        "test_mask  = meta[\"date\"].isin(test_dates)\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train = X.loc[train_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "X_val   = X.loc[val_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "X_test  = X.loc[test_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "y_train = y.loc[train_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "y_val   = y.loc[val_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "y_test  = y.loc[test_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "meta_train = meta.loc[train_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "meta_val   = meta.loc[val_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "meta_test  = meta.loc[test_mask].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Standardize continuous predictors using training data only\n",
        "continuous_features = stock_chars + interaction_cols\n",
        "\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_train[continuous_features] = scaler.fit_transform(X_train[continuous_features])\n",
        "X_val[continuous_features]   = scaler.transform(X_val[continuous_features])\n",
        "X_test[continuous_features]  = scaler.transform(X_test[continuous_features])\n",
        "\n",
        "split_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Sample\": [\"Train\", \"Validation\", \"Test\"],\n",
        "    \"Start date\": [\n",
        "        meta_train[\"date\"].min().date(),\n",
        "        meta_val[\"date\"].min().date(),\n",
        "        meta_test[\"date\"].min().date()\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"End date\": [\n",
        "        meta_train[\"date\"].max().date(),\n",
        "        meta_val[\"date\"].max().date(),\n",
        "        meta_test[\"date\"].max().date()\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Months\": [len(train_dates), len(val_dates), len(test_dates)],\n",
        "    \"Observations\": [len(X_train), len(X_val), len(X_test)]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "split_summary"
      ],
      "id": "30bef614",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The dataset is split chronologically to avoid look-ahead bias, ensuring that training observations precede validation observations, which in turn precede test observations. The most recent 20% of months are reserved as the test set, providing a truly out-of-sample evaluation period.\n",
        "\n",
        "The remaining 80% is split into 75% training and 25% validation, yielding an approximate 60/20/20 split. This reflects a trade-off between reliable parameter estimation and effective model selection.\n",
        "\n",
        "The split is done at the monthly level to preserve the panel structure. Continuous predictors are standardized using the training data only, and the same transformation is applied to validation and test sets to avoid data leakage.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise 2c: Hyperparameter tuning"
      ],
      "id": "7ce95c86"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "import itertools\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import ElasticNet\n",
        "from sklearn.neural_network import MLPRegressor\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import root_mean_squared_error"
      ],
      "id": "a6b17416",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "en_param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"alpha\": [0.001, 0.1],\n",
        "    \"l1_ratio\": [0.2, 0.8],\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "en_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for params in [dict(zip(en_param_grid, v)) for v in itertools.product(*en_param_grid.values())]:\n",
        "    model = ElasticNet(max_iter=5000, fit_intercept=True, **params)\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "    en_results.append({\n",
        "        **params,\n",
        "        \"train_rmse\": root_mean_squared_error(y_train, model.predict(X_train)),\n",
        "        \"val_rmse\": root_mean_squared_error(y_val, model.predict(X_val))\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "en_results_df = pd.DataFrame(en_results).sort_values(\"val_rmse\")\n",
        "\n",
        "best_en_params = en_results_df.iloc[0][[\"alpha\", \"l1_ratio\"]].to_dict()\n",
        "\n",
        "en_results_df.round(6)"
      ],
      "id": "9aa40e04",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "nn_param_grid = {\n",
        "    \"hidden_layer_sizes\": [(32, 16)],\n",
        "    \"alpha\": [0.001, 0.01],\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "nn_results = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for params in [dict(zip(nn_param_grid, v)) for v in itertools.product(*nn_param_grid.values())]:\n",
        "    model = MLPRegressor(\n",
        "        activation=\"relu\",\n",
        "        solver=\"adam\",\n",
        "        max_iter=50,\n",
        "        random_state=42,\n",
        "        **params\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "    nn_results.append({\n",
        "        \"hidden_layers\": str(params[\"hidden_layer_sizes\"]),\n",
        "        \"alpha\": params[\"alpha\"],\n",
        "        \"train_rmse\": root_mean_squared_error(y_train, model.predict(X_train)),\n",
        "        \"val_rmse\": root_mean_squared_error(y_val, model.predict(X_val))\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "nn_results_df = pd.DataFrame(nn_results).sort_values(\"val_rmse\")\n",
        "best_nn_params = nn_results_df.iloc[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "nn_results_df.round(6)"
      ],
      "id": "a1a71829",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "import ast\n",
        "\n",
        "# Fit final models\n",
        "final_en = ElasticNet(\n",
        "    alpha=best_en_params[\"alpha\"],\n",
        "    l1_ratio=best_en_params[\"l1_ratio\"],\n",
        "    max_iter=5000,\n",
        "    fit_intercept=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "final_en.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "best_hidden = ast.literal_eval(best_nn_params[\"hidden_layers\"])\n",
        "final_nn = MLPRegressor(\n",
        "    hidden_layer_sizes=best_hidden,\n",
        "    alpha=best_nn_params[\"alpha\"],\n",
        "    activation=\"relu\",\n",
        "    solver=\"adam\",\n",
        "    max_iter=50,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "final_nn.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
