        "Stocks are sorted into decile portfolios each month based on predicted excess returns. Within each month, stocks are ranked and divided into ten groups of approximately equal size, from the lowest (decile 0) to the highest (decile 9).\n",
        "\n",
        "To ensure stable portfolio formation, predictions are ranked before applying quantile sorting, avoiding issues with tied values. Months with very few observations are excluded.\n",
        "\n",
        "This procedure generates a cross-sectional ranking that reflects the model’s expected return signal and is used to construct long-short portfolios.\n",
        "\n",
